    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0429" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8–1748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Touchette</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-17T12:00:00+09:00">August 17,
                            1948—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 17—4:45 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>308. Remytel August 17, 460 Nanking, 307 Washington and 327 Shanghai.</p>
                <p>As far as could be ascertained this date, purpose North China political military
                    conference is desire Fu Tso-yi to gather opinions leaders of provinces Hopei,
                    Jehol, Chahar, Suiyuan and mayors Peiping and Tientsin and North China military
                    leaders for formation better plans and execution Communist suppression
                    activities these provinces.</p>
                <pb facs="0430" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>
                <p>Vice President Li Tsung-jen attending conference, departing by air noon August 17
                    for Nanking.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 461, Dept 308.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Touchette</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
